                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{gluespokes}:\prod_{x:A} \prod_{i:I} \mathrm{in}(i, f(i, x)) = \mathrm{gluehubs}(x)
          %p
            This is an example of the hubs-and-spokes construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+types"} higher inductive types
            discussed in the
